{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":63428,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"7e0bf9c0-151a-51a0-ab39-01fff2040191","total_cost_usd":0.5357090000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10321,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6493,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10321,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6493,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10321,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10321},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4524,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004619,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":6493,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":10321,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5310900000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-d-reviewer-fable-22\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:7da68ec265e1bb2f6640\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The data description declares the stand as the independent unit, one row per stand, with stand_id unique across the file.\",\"observed_value\":\"One row = one stand; independent unit column stand_id; IDs ST-01 through ST-24 unique\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":15,\"end_line\":16,\"quoted_text\":\"One row is: one surveyed spruce stand, described by the single pooled ingrowth-bag composite collected in that stand\\nIndependent unit column: stand_id\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":20,\"end_line\":20,\"quoted_text\":\"- stand_id: the code of the stand, unique across the file (ST-01 through ST-24).\"}]},{\"description\":\"The CSV contains exactly 24 data rows with 24 distinct stand_id values (ST-01 through ST-24); no stand occupies more than one row, so no independent unit enters the row-level test more than once. Verified by inspection of every row.\",\"observed_value\":{\"data_rows\":24,\"distinct_stand_ids\":24,\"duplicated_stand_ids\":0},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":3,\"quoted_text\":\"stand_id,canopy_state,elevation_m,bags_pooled,hyphal_ingrowth_mg\\nST-01,intact,1180,4,40\\nST-02,gap,1245,4,27\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":24,\"end_line\":25,\"quoted_text\":\"ST-23,gap,1356,4,23\\nST-24,intact,1052,4,42\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow actively enforces one row per independent unit: read_stands raises a ValueError if any stand_id appears twice, so duplicated units cannot reach the test.\",\"observed_value\":\"Uniqueness guard on stand_id before analysis\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":30,\"end_line\":32,\"quoted_text\":\"    stands = [row[UNIT_KEY] for row in rows]\\n    if len(set(stands)) != len(stands):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"a stand is listed more than once; one row per stand is required\\\")\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":17,\"end_line\":17,\"quoted_text\":\"UNIT_KEY = \\\"stand_id\\\"\"}]},{\"description\":\"The row-independent procedure (Welch two-sample t-test) is applied to the deduplicated stand-level rows, one value per stand per group (12 vs 12).\",\"observed_value\":\"stats.ttest_ind on 12 intact and 12 gap stand-level values\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":69,\"end_line\":71,\"quoted_text\":\"    rows = read_stands(DATA_PATH)\\n    a = ingrowth(rows, REFERENCE)\\n    b = ingrowth(rows, CONTRAST)\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":80,\"end_line\":80,\"quoted_text\":\"    tstat, pvalue = stats.ttest_ind(a, b, equal_var=False)\"}]},{\"description\":\"The reported statistics are consistent with exactly one entry per stand: n = 12 per group (24 stands total), group means 41 and 28 mg match hand-computed means of the 12 unique stand values per group, and t = 6.5 with df = 22 follows from those 24 values.\",\"observed_value\":{\"n_intact\":12,\"n_gap\":12,\"mean_intact_mg\":41,\"mean_gap_mg\":28,\"t\":6.5,\"df\":22},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":23,\"end_line\":23,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Welch's two-sample t-test on 12 intact-canopy stands versus 12 canopy-gap stands: mean difference 13.000 mg (intact minus gap), 95% CI [8.85, 17.15] mg, SE 2.000 mg, t = 6.5000, df = 22.00, two-sided p < 0.0001; mycelial ingrowth is higher in intact-canopy stands.\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":12,\"end_line\":13,\"quoted_text\":\"| intact | 12 | 41.000 | 4.899 | 41.000 |\\n| gap | 12 | 28.000 | 4.899 | 28.500 |\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"Potential concern probed: each stand's composite derives from four ingrowth bags (bags_pooled = 4), which could constitute repeated sub-unit measurements. However, the description states the bags were physically merged and weighed once before entering the file, so the sub-unit replication never appears as separate rows and cannot enter the test repeatedly; bags_pooled is constant bookkeeping, not a repeated measurement.\",\"observed_value\":\"bags_pooled = 4 on every row; pooling occurred before weighing\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":9,\"end_line\":13,\"quoted_text\":\"buried in the organic horizon in June and lifted in September. The four bags\\nfrom a stand were combined into a single composite sample in the field, and that\\none composite was dried and weighed once in the laboratory. A stand therefore\\nyields exactly one ingrowth number, and it occupies exactly one line of the\\nfile.\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":30,\"end_line\":32,\"quoted_text\":\"Nothing in the file is a repeated measurement of the same stand. The bags were\\nmerged before weighing, so the file holds 24 measurements from 24 stands, and a\\ntwo-group comparison across rows compares independent stands.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I tried to demonstrate the issue by (1) scanning all 24 data rows of data/input.csv for any duplicated stand_id value — none exists, ST-01 through ST-24 each appear exactly once; (2) checking whether the workflow re-enters any row into the test (e.g., concatenation, per-bag expansion, or resampling) — ingrowth() filters the deduplicated rows once per group and stats.ttest_ind receives 12 and 12 values, and read_stands would raise on any duplicated stand_id; (3) checking whether the four bags per stand could act as repeated entries of the stand — the description states bags were physically pooled into one composite weighed once, so per-bag values never exist as rows; (4) recomputing the summary statistics from the 24 unique rows (intact mean 41, gap mean 28, difference 13, SE 2, t = 6.5, df = 22, both group SDs 4.899) — all match the report, which would not hold if any unit had been counted more than once. Every attempt failed to produce evidence of repeated independent-unit entry.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-d-reviewer-fable-22","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:7da68ec265e1bb2f6640","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_state